## Quick Reference: OWASP API Security Top 10 (2024)

| # | Category | Mitigation |
|---|----------|------------|
| 1 | **API1:2024 – Broken Object Level Authorization** | Enforce server‑side ACLs, validate object IDs against user context |
| 2 | **API2:2024 – Broken Authentication** | OAuth 2.0, PKCE, strong password policies, MFA |
| 3 | **API3:2024 – Excessive Data Exposure** | Minimum‑necessary data, field‑level masking |
| 4 | **API4:2024 – Lack of Resources & Rate Limiting** | Token bucket, quotas, dynamic throttling |
| 5 | **API5:2024 – Broken Function Level Authorization** | Scope checks, endpoint‑level RBAC |
| 6 | **API6:2024 – Mass Assignment** | Strong schema validation, allowlist only |
| 7 | **API7:2024 – Security Misconfiguration** | Harden defaults, secure API gateway, disable debug |
| 8 | **API8:2024 – Injection** | Parameterize queries, use ORM, sanitize inputs |
| 9 | **API9:2024 – Improper Assets Management** | Versioning, deprecation, remove unused endpoints |
| 10 | **API10:2024 – Insufficient Logging & Monitoring** | Centralized logging, alerting, audit trails |

